;; Problem statements, one per stage of the run, written before the stage is built (docs/RICH-HICKEY.md,
;; "And the hammock."): the problem, the information it needs that the bot does not yet gather, what
;; can go wrong, what done means in world terms, and what the last recorded failure showed. Hand-written
;; data next to goals.edn; problems_test requires a statement for every target goal and checks every
;; source exists. Stages already built cite our own recorded failures; stages ahead cite the siblings
;; (steve, ruststeve), whose notes in brain/siblings are research drafts until re-verified.
;; Update a row when a run of that stage fails in a new way: the failure is the most valuable line here.
[{:problem/stage :wood
  :problem/goals [:wood]
  :problem/statement
  "Hold one log from a natural tree, starting wherever the bot lands, with only what the server has sent it."
  :problem/needs
  ["Which loaded blocks are logs, and which log of a trunk is at feet height."
   "Where its own drop is, and whether a leaf covers it."
   "Whether the landing itself is usable: not water, not inside a canopy, not buried."]
  :problem/risks
  ["A drop lands under the trunk, out of a 1.8-tall player's reach."
   "A branch passes for a trunk bottom, or the trunk stands on a bank above the bot: the drop rests out of the pickup box."
   "A leaf at head height hides the drop and walking cannot pass it."
   "The fixture lands the bot on a pond, in a canopy or in stone."
   "An early FINISH aborts the break."]
  :problem/done "The server's inventory read for the bot shows any *_log."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Recorded in CI and replayed: collect failed :not-picked-up when the bot dug the base log from two blocks above (fixed by trunk-target), and again when a low oak leaf covered the drop (fixed by digging the blocker). Recorded live 2026-10-10 on a pickaxe run and diagnosed by folding the recording: three collects in a row failed :not-picked-up because the drop lay one block up a ledge with leaves one above head height over the ledge and over the bot, so no jump rose a full block (fixed: over a one-block step, the blocker also looks one above the head, in both columns). Recorded by the gym (batch wood-a2 run 5) and again by a plan (smoke2 run 5), landing 21280,18720, and diagnosed by folding the recording: the bot took a branch log (air under it) for a trunk bottom and its drop came to rest on the trunk below; then, standing in a pit, it dug the real base on a bank four blocks above its feet and that drop rested above its pickup box; each failed walk blacklisted one log, not the tree, so it kept choosing the same trunk until the plan failed :stuck. Fixed: a trunk bottom stands on ground (or over its own dug base), a log walk arrives only with the drop's resting height within pickup reach of the feet, and a failed log intent blacklists its whole trunk (sim scenarios a-drop-out-of-reach-is-never-dug-for and a-trunk-on-a-bank-is-taken-from-the-bank). The forest property now generates branches and banks 1-2 high; a tree on a 2-high bank holds its drop beyond a pickup from the ground, and the bot gives it up (:no-log when it is the only tree). Race 38674091115 (issue #87) climbed it instead: out is not at the trees, and a trunk remembered above the eye no walk reaches is now climbed toward (wood/trees-climb), the forest property now accepts a 2-high bank when the climb succeeds (world {:x 13, :z 3, :h 3, :mound 2} seed 386881739251), while retaining :no-log for unsupported banks. The walk now follows a planned route (issue #4): a pond or a two-block ledge between the bot and the trunk, which ended :stuck and blacklisted the trunk, is routed around or climbed by its step (sim scenario a-log-across-a-cliff-and-a-pond-is-reached-by-a-route). Race 38477665442 (issue #38, 39 bots, and the sim race in the same worlds): every bot landed on snowy ground never moved, twelve walks failing :no-path in a second, because one layer of snow lay on every block round it and a route took that layer for an awkward shape, so neither the feet cell nor any beside it could be stood on and every plan was :none from nowhere. Fixed: one layer of snow has no collision shape in the game and the physics passes through it, so a route does too (path/one-layer-snow; path-test a-snowfield-is-crossed-through-its-one-layer-snow). Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, issue #57, 20 real runs): bots Clj_r14 and Clj_r20 and their runners' twins landed on a lake's shore with every remembered trunk across the water; each walk at one failed :no-path, and once every trunk in reach was given up the gather waited :no-log until the plan failed, the forest beyond the hill never loaded. Under the open sky with no route to any trunk the gather now hunts toward the nearest log, as a water hunt goes out, forty blocks at a time (wood/hunt). Race 38665691517 (issue #57): landings with no standing trunk in reach waited :no-log at the landing round after round, routes out on three bearings; the wood hunt now sets out with no log known (wood/hunt). Race 38680745815 runner 5 (issue #57, 2026-10-15): under server load the planner now counts waits in ticks, and a hunt with remembered trees can walk toward them after leaving the landing. Sim race 38811417241 runner 2 (issue #87, world R2/20): out of the mine on a block in a powder-snow field, powder snow neither floor nor clear to a route left no move toward a spruce eight blocks off and the plan waited :no-log at the ingots; powder snow is passable now (no collision for a player), routes go through it, and climb-out asks only the nearest logs whether they are standing trunks. Same round (world R3/4): on a sand island at its landing with every trunk a hundred blocks across a lake and every hunt bearing at water, the plan waited :no-log; it now swims across toward the nearest remembered trunk (wood/crossing, swim :cross). Sim race 38844589684 runner 6 (issue #57, world R1/30 seed 4): on a sand headland with the trees across a lake, the crossing swam forty blocks and stuck eight short against a far bank too high to climb, failing :stuck three times; a crossing stuck in the water now swims for the nearest bank and ends there."
  :problem/sources
  ["brain/bot/gotchas/drop-under-the-trunk.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/leaf-canopy-over-the-drop.md"
   "brain/bot/tooling/harness-landing.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/early-finish-aborts.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :kit
  :problem/issue 2
  :problem/goals [:kit]
  :problem/statement
  "Turn logs into a crafting table and four sticks through the 2x2 grid, believing only what the server says the window holds."
  :problem/needs
