  :problem/goals [:portal-kit :cast-one :portal :nether]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot must cast ten obsidian blocks from lava and water into a nether portal frame, light it and stand in it, the way a player does: beside any lava pool at any depth, each frame cell a hole cut into the rock, lava poured in and water poured straight over it and scooped back, never mining obsidian (issue #124)."
  :problem/needs
  ["A site beside a lava pool whose frame, room and floors hold no fluid and touch none, with the lava's stand over the room's floor"
   "Loaded lava sources at any depth, a stand beside the cell over one, and the blocks the plan places where the rock is missing"
   "The server's block-update for every place and pour, never a local prediction"
   "Which ops of the build plan are already satisfied, so a resume skips them"
   "The current dimension, from the respawn packet"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Lava pour lands outside the hole: the ray enters the frame below the cell (a stand too low or too far aside)"
   "Water poured beside the lava instead of over it: the source flows into the water and leaves cobblestone"
   "Water aimed at the floor replaces the lava source instead of making obsidian"
   "Scooping late lets water spread and convert the lava pool"
   "Placing into a lava source destroys it; casting over a lava sea has no stance"
   "A rejected placement left as a ghost block; the pathfinder digs finished obsidian"
   "Lighting with the hitbox in the fire cell burns the bot"]
  :problem/done
  "Ten obsidian frame blocks and nether_portal blocks inside exist (RCON execute if block), and after standing in the portal RCON data get entity Dimension reads the Nether."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The mold is cast in the model from the kit to the Nether, resumed over six cells already cast and after a death; live cast-one passed 5/5 on the runners (batch p1-cast-one). The last failure, in the model: the site was chosen at the landing, so a death respawned the bot inside its own frame's corner and every walk out failed :no-path (vanilla never respawns a player inside blocks; a natural site near the world spawn still could put the frame over it). Before: ruststeve's blocker was casting over a lava sea and lidded cups bending pours onto the feet; steve went natural 0/63 versus arena 66/72, the wall being lava refill reachability. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 4e59246): at the pond with flint and steel, a water bucket and the portal kit, the pad's stand was stone inside the hill and three walks at it failed :no-path. The solid between the feet and a stand is dug. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, f277605): flint and steel, a water bucket and 283 cobblestone, then five hours walking out of the iron mine for a spare pickaxe and cutting back down. The mouth was under the sky and no trunk could be walked to. A walk up the dug shaft is not a spare; the mine continues, and the empty bucket the portal kit still needs can be smelted. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, 61abf8c): flint and steel, a water bucket and 334 cobblestone at the pond, portal kit reached. The cast's first open pad cell was water and the stand for it was air over the next water cell; the walk there was :partial six times and three :no-path failures ended the plan. A place whose stand cannot be occupied is made from a cell that already reaches the block. Full run on a fresh world (2026-10-12, ab3945e): a furnace and a stone pickaxe reached, then at y 32 every stair and every further level step was refused and three :stairs-down failures :boxed ended the plan. The cell a descent dies on is not stair'd again; the mine leaves it. Sim race 38395033917 (2026-10-13, world R3/24, 108 runs, issue #75): the portal kit wanted an empty bucket and 47 more cobblestone; the bot cut two staircases for stone, the second from the bottom of the first, and the second's first step dug out the first's riser, so no route led up (the :sky plan :none). Then, for the wood a new table needed, every walk to a trunk within the near band failed :no-path the tick it started and blacklisted that trunk, twelve a second, until the plan failed. A trunk in the band is now asked for a route before it is walked at, as the far ones were, so the bot climbs out instead (wood/near-walk). Open: a staircase cut from the bottom of another should not take the riser of the way back up. Race 38477665442 (issue #45, 18 real bots a round at cast-one): Clj_r25 scooped its water from a sand cell at a lake's edge under a bank two high; the pad's stand was over the water, the cell nearest it was the bank's top, which only cells over the water led to, and three builds failed :no-path walking at it while the sand cell itself reached the pad. Fixed: the stand chosen in the designated one's place is the nearest a route reaches (build-test a-stand-up-a-bank-is-passed-over-for-one-a-route-reaches). Clj_r06 built at y 16 in its iron mine with the only lava remembered sealed in rock fourteen blocks off: the refill's walk to that station has no route and tunnelling to it is not done yet. Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, issue #43): bot Clj_r04 held the kit and 488 cobblestone and wanted the empty bucket; its redig for flint had failed :not-picked-up at the cell before its feet, the table for a spare pickaxe went into that cell, and as a blacklisted position it did not count as near, so the bot went for the wood of a new table with its last pickaxe, found no route, climbed, and under a bed of gravel at y 42 stepped thirty cells along it, every stair refused, until the pickaxe broke. A place or a redig blacklists nothing now, and a climb steps out from under gravel before along it. Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, 28 real bots, issue #49): the portal kit was reached while its only bucket was still empty, the water bucket filled after it, and the cast waited :no-bucket with no empty bucket for the lava; a reached step is never asked again, so the kit now counts the water bucket beside the empty one. Sim race 38477665389 (issue #91, 54 runs, world R1/27): the site's station was a lava source under stone, and the refill's scoop at it failed :target-gone three times; the same race's real bots had the station's distance measured on the plane alone, so the sea ninety blocks down counted. A station is now within sixteen in all three dimensions and open to the air above. Sim race 38395033917 and race 38477665442 (issue #74, 211 sim runs and 3 real bots): a pad cell over a cave or a deep pond, its stand air over the drop, had no cell within a foundation's four blocks to build it from and no standable cell in reach of the block, :no-stand three times. A site now has no water in its footprint and ground under every pad cell no deeper than a foundation reaches. Race 38477665442 and sim race 38477665389 (issue #41, the most frequent failure past the kit: 47 real bots, 950 sim runs at 16 landings): the bot stood at the surface with the kit, no lava within sixteen of any origin, and waited :no-site out; lava is nowhere on the surface of a 1.18+ world, it is the sea under y -54 under a deepslate ceiling, and cave springs. With no site the planner now hunts: a walk to a stand beside an exposed source, stairs and a tunnel toward the nearest source loaded, the roof over it dug from a cell beside it, and the site chosen there; in rock the lid over each bowl is dug too, since the water's ray clipped it and the pour landed on the bot's head, and the rim never fills the station's stand. Sim race 38477665389 (issue #70, 150 runs, world R1/14): the cast dug for its stance with no pickaxe left, every stone refused :needs-tool, three times. The build rows now hold a pickaxe, made by the needs planner before the build starts, and the gym's portal kit gives one. Sim race 38515210080 (issue #71, 74 runs, world R3/16 at y 48): the cobblestone for the mold wanted, the mine stood on a dirt spur between a lake and a cave with its feet cell in :plan/boxed-at, no tunnel heading and no retreat, and waited :boxed out. Its snapshots (test/issues/71) play on past it since the staircase deeper casts its floors through the cave (issue #37); they are kept as the check. Sim race 38477665389 (issue #92, 48 runs, world R2/23 at the portal kit): the bucket filled from a pond's edge, the bot stood in the one of water its source had left, its eye in air, and the mine for the mold's cobblestone, with nothing to cut from the water, retreated by a swim-out that found no bank in its band (the shore two over the feet), no cap over the head, and held jump until it timed out, three times, :no-escape. The notch cut for the flooded cave (issue #73) takes the shore the same way; a-retreat-from-a-scooped-ponds-edge-notches-the-bank holds that moment. Sim race 38477665389 (issue #94, 11 runs, world R1/43 at the portal kit): the furnace for the bucket's ingots at the end of an iron tunnel at y 16, the table behind it in the passage, two stone pickaxes held and :no-spot three times; the hotbar was full of what mining picked up, so equipping the furnace swapped the pickaxe into the main inventory, and the niche, asked of the hotbar alone, refused every stone wall as a block the tools cannot drop. A pickaxe stowed in the main inventory now counts, and the niche's dig puts it in hand first. Issue #124 (every round, every bot with the kit stopped at cast-one: no-site, no-bucket, no-path, never one obsidian outside the arena): the mold asked for a flat, dry, loaded footprint with a station near and 192 cobblestone. The cast is now cut into the rock beside any lava pool: holes in a rock face, lava in, water straight over, the room dug in front, four blocks in solid rock, the blocks counted from the plan for the place chosen. Race 38650995686 (issue #131): the portal kit's crafts failed :stale-window on one late answer from a loaded server; a lost click is now resynced and the intent goes on (window/lost). Sim race 38664661309 (issue #142, 89 runs): sites beside a lone lava source cast one cell and stopped :no-station; a site now needs a pool its stands reach with a source for every cell (build/spent?), and a spent site is left for a new one. Sim race 38665691522 (issue #44): a floor was laid from a stand whose head was in its cell and refused three times, :rejected; a stand never covers the cell worked on now, and a placement refused for the bot's own body is approached again (build/refused-for-the-body?). Sim race 38660819204 (issue #74): the bot stood outside its own room with no route in and failed :no-stand; the build now cuts its way to a stand at the feet's height (build/nearest-stand-cell), though the frame's rock between the feet and the room is not yet gone round. Sim race 38665691522 (issue #71): a bot with no pickaxe, climbing out for wood from under water, was :boxed three times; since a boxed climb to the surface ends and is not cut from that cell again (stairs/box, issue #61) the same moment stops at [:portal-kit :no-log] instead (issue #89). Sim races 38660819204, 38662908438 and 38665691522 (issue #94, worlds R1/44, R1/13, R1/37): the furnace for the kit's ingots was to go down at the dead end of an iron tunnel at y 9-17 by an aquifer, every wall beside the feet touched water or had the passage over it, and the place failed :no-spot three times; a place with nowhere now walks once to fresh rock twelve blocks away and looks again (place/fresh-rock). Sim race 38665691522 world R3/43 (issue #91): the way to the cast's landing at y 24 dug an awkward block over the feet, the dig took anything not solid for open and failed :target-gone, and the build failed with it; now only air or a fluid is open (intent/open?), and a dig that finds its cell open makes way for the next child (build/found-open?). Sim race 38806318231 (issue #70, 1065 runs in 197 rounds): the cast's room met deepslate redstone ore with a wooden pickaxe, and the way to a landing was dug by hand with the spare stone pickaxe stowed in slot 35 until iron ore in it, each dig refused :needs-tool three times; a build's digs now break ore they cannot harvest for nothing (build/way-dig, :intent/drop-ok?) and put a stowed pickaxe in hand first (build/tool-first). Sim race 38806318231 (issue #130, world R3/11): the stairs down to the cast's landing at y -22 met an aquifer at y 11, every stair refused, and the build sent the same stairs down from the same cell three times, :boxed; a boxed way is now remembered in :plan/boxed-at and dropped, and from the pocket the build takes the way out (stone/retreat, stone/climb) before the next descent (build/work-op, build/to-height). Sim race 38715231137 (issue #142, regressed, 166 runs in 44 rounds): at the station the nearest source had flowing lava or rock over it, the line to it already clear, and the refill, asking for air over the source, failed :no-station three times in three ticks with half the pool left; the scoop is now aimed along the line and needs only the source, and a source behind obsidian gives way to the next (build/scoop-at-station). Sim race 38665691522 and a probe at 8356e28 (issue #162, world R3/37): the refill's way out from the landing to the lava's stand ran over a cave's open cell beside the room, the line clear and nothing to dig, and the walk, with no floor to stand on, failed :no-path three times; a way at the feet's height over a hole now gets a cobblestone floor first (build/bridge). Sim races 38806318231 runner 1 and 38811426215 runner 8 (issue #89, worlds R4/30, R4/21 and R1/32 at 76010d2) mined under the sea floor until the last pickaxe broke, then needed a log with every climb out boxed under the water and waited :no-log; boxed there the gather now digs up into the sea, rises up the shaft and swims for the nearest shore or the landing. Sim race 38806318231 (issue #161, 206 runs in 73 rounds, world R1/37 at the portal kit): the spare pickaxe's gather climbed from the iron mine to the surface, found no tree in reach, the mine cut stairs back down, and the gather climbed again, every twenty seconds until the ninety minutes ran out; a spare's climb is now declined from under where a climb came out in the last ten minutes (make/spare-worth?, stairs/surfaced-near?). The same issue in world R3/7: three planks short of the bucket's table, 36 slots full of cobblestone, stones, sand, lapis and copper, the bot dug log after log and every collect timed out :not-picked-up; a row that goes out for something now throws junk first when no slot is free (make/make-room, the :toss intent). Sim race at 76010d2 (issue #45, world R4/33, 2540 runs of the signature in 365 rounds): the bot stood behind its own frame with the landing straight ahead through the frame's rock, which no way digs; the cells past the rock were dug, the landing stayed out of reach and three walks at it failed :no-path; the way now goes round the rock by a corner (build/round-corner). Sim race 38837004562 (issue #45, world R1/6): the level way to the landing at y 21 ran under a bed of gravel, each dug cell filled again and three walks along it failed :no-path; such a walk is now dropped and the way cleared again (build/way-refilled?). Race 38839564087 runner 1 (issue #225, at 3f836ff): three bots sent nine lava scoops each from the station along lines grazing a block's edge, which the server's ray hit, and the build failed :no-scoop; the refill's line is now the thick ray and its aim moves a quarter block off the centre when that ray is blocked. Sim race 38839665459 (issue #222, world R1/11): the cast kept a site 70 blocks off across an aquifer, the walk there failed :no-path, the swim out of the water the stairs toward it let in :stuck, and the escape :stuck; a way to the site that fails :no-path or :stuck from far off now gives the site up, and the next is chosen elsewhere (build/lost-way?, memory/give-up-site). Sim race 38839665459 runner 3 (issue #71, world R1/19 at 3f836ff) cut stairs down to y 1 for the bucket's iron and tunnelled back under them, undermining its only way up; boxed beside an aquifer it failed :boxed; a tunnel never heads back under the stairs just cut. Sim races 38806318231 and 38843552659 (issue #186, worlds R1/25, R2/11, R1/18, R4/39): the cast wore out every pickaxe with sticks and cobblestone in hand and the table left at the furnace, the bot went out for a log from a ravine's floor or a boxed climb and waited :no-log with trees remembered sixty blocks off; a build now takes the placed table along or makes one for its kit from what is held (build/carry-table?), and the wood hunt takes the way out of a pit or a pocket before waiting (wood/way-out). Sim race 38855091523 at 5d78c91 (issue #178, world R1/34 seed 2): with the table carried (#186) the run got to the portal, but the lava's stand at y -53 was still stone; a route led beside it, the walk ended a block under it, and the refill went back to the landing, out again and back, three walks every five seconds until the time ran out; a stand in the rock is now cut to, never walked near (build/stand-walk), and from beside it the way is to its height (build/beside-stand?). The same run then walked between the far side of the lava it had opened and the landing, the straight way crossing the lava; the refill now goes out along the landing's column only when that way is clear of lava and the feet are not beside the stand already (build/out-first?). Then the walk to the block in the way ended a block under it, in a hole of the floor, and the refill went back to the landing; the block is now dug from the hole when in reach (build/dig-from-under). Sim race 38843557186 runner 3 (issues #231, #228, world R1/31): the build's way to a landing at the lava sea's height was dug along the sea's edge, a cell beside a source opened, the lava flowed in, and no footing was in reach, :no-footing; a way never opens a cell beside lava now (build/diggable?, build/barred). World R3/12 seed 1 from spawn on main (Refs #178): the cast wore out the pickaxes holding a table, 684 cobblestone and one plank but no sticks, and the bot cut stairs up through deepslate by hand for a log until its ninety minutes ran out; a build now carries two sticks beside the table when what is held makes them (build/carry-sticks?)."
