 {:problem/stage :nether-and-fortress
  :problem/issue 11
  :problem/goals [:fortress]
  :problem/statement
  "The world value is overworld-only, so after a portal the bot cannot tell which dimension it is in, decodes Nether chunks with the wrong height, and has no safe way to reach a fortress across the lava sea."
  :problem/needs
  ["The dimension from login and respawn (sent as a registry index, 3 = the_nether)"
   "Per-dimension chunk height: Nether is min-y 0, 16 sections; overworld -64, 24 sections"
   "Sightings keyed by dimension, watching nether_bricks, spawner, portal, obsidian and lava"
   "Real chunk data after arrival before any step runs, not a timer"
   "Lava next to each tunnel step and missing floors ahead"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Chunks stay a snapshot of the dimension the bot is in, emptied on a change, as the server streams them again; memory keeps every dimension, each fact saying which"
   "A column's height is the sections the server sent (16 or 24), looked up in dimensions.edn: the reader thread decodes without knowing the dimension"
   "The dimension is the respawn's and login's name (:player/dimension, from #8), not the registry id, which only dimensions.edn's row order explains"
   "No lava capping: a cell behind a wall cannot be capped before the wall is dug, so a tunnel step never opens a cell beside lava and tries another step instead"
   "The gym gives a row's kit only once the server says the bot stands in the row's dimension (execute as <bot> at @s if dimension): steve gave its End kit before the cross-dimension teleport and the server held none of it (issue #261)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Stale overworld columns answer Nether lookups (a brick reported exactly 64 blocks off)"
   "Parsing a Nether chunk as 24 sections runs off the buffer"
   "Overworld goals (mine iron) run in the Nether"
   "Falling into the lava sea on an open approach to the fortress"
   "Fortress brick picked below the lava sea surface"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON confirms the bot is in minecraft:the_nether with nether_bricks under its feet or within 6 blocks, RESULT :ok true, and zero deaths counted."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never attempted this. ruststeve: after entering the Nether its overworld columns answered Nether lookups (fortress brick reported 64 blocks too low) and the parser panicked on the shorter Nether chunk; finding the fortress was solved, but reaching it alive was not, with 9+ falls into the lava sea at one spot."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/09-nether-and-fortress.md" "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dimension-change.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :survival
  :problem/issue 259
  :problem/goals [:eat :wear-armour :armour :defend :attack :hunt :sword]
  :problem/statement
  "Normal difficulty brings hunger and night mobs to every stage. Food drains with every dig and jump, an empty bar stops healing and starves the bot to one heart, and zombies, skeletons and creepers find a bot that cannot hit back. The world value read the health from set-health and threw the food away; the bot could not eat, wear armour or attack."
  :problem/needs
  ["The food level from set-health (decoded since the packet was specced, never kept)"
   "Which food is safe to eat and how long eating takes: the game's food properties"
   "The 775 attack packet and every mob tracked with its health (issue #258)"
   "A sword in hand for every fight, and armour worn through window-0 clicks into the armour slots"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Eating is an always row at priority 0 after the escapes, done when fed (food 14 or more) or when nothing edible is held, so a hungry bot with no food goes on with the run"
   "The meal is the server's food rising; a deadline from the food's eating time, stretched by the server's slowdown, fails it :not-eaten"
   "Never eat what poisons or makes hungry, chorus fruit, suspicious stew or golden apples"
   "A fight is its own intent (:fight): the 775 attack packet, the look set a tick before, attacks 650 ms apart by the clock (a deadline on the intent), a kill when the target is gone, a ghost after 25 swings in reach, broken off under 10 health; :defend is an always row after the escapes (a hostile within 4, a creeper within 6 backed away from); the gym's :attack is an aside, never a step of a chained run"
   "Food is produced by :hunt, an always row after the meal: hungry with nothing edible, walk to the nearest cow, pig, sheep or rabbit a route reaches within 24, fight it, collect its meat where it fell, eat it raw; never chickens"
   "The sword is the :sword always row after the armour: iron from ingots the armour leaves, else stone from cobblestone, else wood from planks, never from a log, so it takes nothing the pickaxes need; until it is made the fights are by hand"
   "Armour is put on by two window-0 clicks (pick up, put down in the armour slot) and made only from ingots spare once the portal's iron is held, with a table at hand: it never sends the bot mining or after a tree"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A meal preempts work mid-intent: a smelt abandoned leaves its input in the furnace"
   "Another slot selected mid-meal stops the eating (set-carried-item)"
   "Nothing edible held: the bar stays empty until a food producer (passive animals killed) exists"
   "Swings inside a mob's 10-tick hurt invulnerability do nothing"
   "A creeper fought instead of fled"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: the bot's foodLevel at 14 or more after landing hungry with bread, and fewer breads held; a NoAI zombie gone with the attacks 650 ms apart; three zombies at night survived."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never eaten or fought: every server ran Peaceful until #257 set Normal. ruststeve spent sessions dealing no damage (interact instead of attack, 40 swings in 66 ms) before its blaze kills."
  :problem/sources ["docs/RICH-HICKEY.md" "brain/siblings/sib-775-attack-packet.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-blaze-combat.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :end-and-dragon
  :problem/issue 10
  :problem/statement
  "Everything after the Nether (blaze rods, pearls, eyes, stronghold, End portal, dragon) has never been crossed naturally by any bot, and the world value has no mob model, no combat packets and no way to follow a thrown eye."
  :problem/needs
  ["Every mob in the entity map with velocity and health (health from set-entity-data)"
   "The 775 attack packet spec and the pose synced one tick before attacking"
   "Eye of ender flight positions after each throw, to triangulate the stronghold"
   "Which end portal frames still lack an eye"
   "Server-side win signal: dragon entity removed, advancement, or credits game event"
   "Server difficulty: Peaceful has no blazes, piglins, endermen or dragon fight"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Attacking via interact deals no damage, or a hand-less interact gets the bot kicked"
   "Swings inside the 10-tick hurt invulnerability do nothing"
   "Wither skeletons or fireballs kill the bot mid-fight" "Looking at an enderman turns it hostile"
   "Kit given before the cross-dimension teleport is missing server-side"
   "Dragon not in view mistaken for a win"]
