 {:problem/stage :blaze-rods
  :problem/issue 262
  :problem/goals [:blaze-rods]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. Seven blaze rods (six for the twelve blaze powder the eyes of ender take, one spare), from blazes a fortress's spawner makes, without dying to their fireballs: the first stage past the fortress, and the first whose loot may not come (a rod one kill in two)."
  :problem/needs
  ["Where a blaze spawner is: a spawner seen in the Nether is a fortress's, remembered after its chunk unloads (memory/nether-landmark-kinds)"
   "Which blazes are near and alive, and how hurt the bot is (entity.clj, set-health)"
   "Which drop on the ground is a rod: a dropped item's stack from its metadata (index 8)"
   "A pickup that is done when nothing lies there to pick up, since a kill may drop nothing (:collect-drops)"
   "A fight that reaches a target hovering over the floor (combat/pressing?)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Fireballs: five a hit on Normal, and fire; a bot that fights on under 10 health dies with the blaze (ruststeve)"
   "A blaze hovering out of reach, never attacked"
   "A spawner's delay (natural ones 10 to 40 s) longer than a planner wait, failing a plan that only had to stand there"
   "A rod lying where no walk reaches it: on the spawner, in lava"
   "Wither skeletons beside the spawner" "Peaceful: no blazes at all"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: seven or more blaze rods in the bot's inventory (clear <bot> minecraft:blaze_rod 0), from the nether arena's spawner and from a fortress pad."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Not played yet: the parts land first (issue #262): a drop's stack is read from its metadata, :collect-drops is done when nothing of the item lies near, a Nether spawner is remembered, and an engaged fight walks on toward a target hovering out of reach. Then the goal (blaze.clj) and its gym rows: blaze-1 (invulnerable, six rods given) passed 3/3 twice (runs 38891907112, 38893160457). blaze-7 (not invulnerable) died twice of three burning in a 7-square room (blaze-7a, run 38891910129) and stalled once when fire by the spawner lit its floor past light 11, so the spawner made no blaze for three minutes: the arena now sets mob griefing off and gives Fire Resistance; then 2/3 (blaze-7b), a volley taking 12.7 health in two seconds while the bot fought on hungry (a meal now comes first under 14 health); then 3/5 (blaze-7c), three blazes' volleys at once killing from 16; with one blaze at a time from a slower spawner, 5/5 (blaze-7d, run 38896099962), breaking off under 10 in three runs and eating in four. blaze-fortress (from the fortress pad): every run failed three fights :unreachable on blazes seen through the fortress's walls (blaze-fortress-a; only reachable blazes are fought now), then camped ten minutes in the wall four over the spawner, its blazes out of reach (blaze-fortress-b; a tunnel to a spawner now ends in the open cell beside it, climbing first); then came up three under the spawner's floor and killed eight blazes whose rods lay out of reach over it, while the :defend row chased blazes through walls and over its head (blaze-fortress-c; only blazes in sight and within 3 over or 2 under the feet are fought now, by either row); then reached the cell beside the spawner and died there waiting to heal, burning and shot, in every run of -e, -f and -g (a hurt bot now hides in the nearest cell out of a watching blaze's sight, and the row gives Fire Resistance); blaze-fortress-h (run 38905665758) still 0/3: fights :unreachable three in a row (the fight's approach walks straight, never along a route, and a blaze behind a fortress fence is never reached), the tunnel's step into the spawner's room failing :no-path, and one run slain by volleys. With the slower arena spawner blaze-7 passed 14/15 (blaze-7d, -e, -f) and blaze-1 3/3 in every batch. A fight now approaches along a route once the straight way stalls, engages when the route says it stands as near as it walks, and a tunnel step the feet left is chosen again: blaze-fortress passed for the first time, 2/3 (run 38911617612) and 1/5 (run 38913023560); the rest died to volleys from the natural spawner's bursts, failed fights :unreachable, or timed out at another landing's fortress."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/10-blazes-pearls-stronghold-end.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-blaze-combat.md" "brain/bot/plan/survival.md"
                    "brain/bot/plan/collect-intent.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :sim-mobs-and-end
  :problem/issue 260
  :problem/goals []
  :problem/statement
  "The server model has no hunger, no mobs, no eye of ender and no End, so the sim lanes play an easier game than the real races at Normal, and nothing past the Nether can be played against the model; every stage after the fortress needs the model to play it first."
  :problem/needs
  ["Hunger as FoodData keeps it: exhaustion from jumps, digs, hits and heals, saturation first, regeneration at 18, starvation to 1 health on Normal, eating a held food for 32 ticks"
   "The server's difficulty as an input, absent for snapshots kept before it, so they play as they did"
   "Mobs that spawn by a seeded rule (night, dark cells, a cap), walk straight at the player and hurt it; creepers that fuse and blast; skeletons that shoot at range; an attack that hurts them by the held item and kills them with their loot"
   "Mob fixtures (:sim/mobs given) for every combat stage's sim tests"
   "An eye of ender thrown with use-item that flies toward the stronghold as a real eye does"
   "The End: arrival on the obsidian platform, end portal frames that take eyes and light the portal, a perched dragon with 200 health and crystals on their pillars"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A model that sends a packet shape the bot's specs reject, once the mob model's specs land (#258)"
   "Hunger or mobs in the unit tests' worlds changing what every older test sees"
   "Mob ticks slowing the 2,000-world property or the sim lanes"
   "A model easier than the server (no blast, no arrows) hiding real deaths, or harder (mobs through walls) making false failures"]
  :problem/done
  "sim tests for each mechanic pass against the model, and the sim lanes' runs show deaths and foods eaten (:run/respawns, :run/eaten)."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Not played yet: the sim lanes ran without hunger or mobs while the real races ran at Normal (#257), so a death or an empty bar was a real-only failure. Hunger landed first (PR #270: the bar drains at Normal in every sim lane run); then mobs (night and dark spawns, melee, arrows, creeper blasts, the 775 attack with its hurt window, loot), so a lane run now dies to a zombie as a real one does (mob_test the-bot-killed-by-a-zombie-respawns). Then eyes of ender flown toward :stronghold, frames that light the end portal, and the End (the platform, a perched dragon of 200 health its crystals heal), so the stronghold, portal and dragon stages can be played against the model first (end_test)."
  :problem/sources ["brain/bot/tooling/server-model.md" "docs/RICH-HICKEY.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :mob-model
  :problem/issue 258
